----------
scriptunit-fragment 1
----------

let a = 1000

----------
scriptunit-fragment 2
----------

let d = 0

----------
scriptunit-fragment 3
----------

let a2 = a
let q = 10 /! d

----------
scriptunit-fragment 4
----------

let e = q + 1

----------
expect all four units are entered, and unit 3 returns early
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | compiles, runs | new | `a` moved |
| 2 | - | compiles, runs | new | `d` = 0 |
| 3 | takes `a` (1), reads `d` (2) | compiles, returns early | `10 /! 0` | - |
| 4 | reads `q` (3) | compiles, is blocked | unit 3 did not finish | - |

----------
scriptunit-edit 2
----------

let d = 5

----------
expect unit 2 is edited so unit 3 finishes
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 3 took `a` when it last ran, and reruns | `a` moved |
| 2 | - | recompiles, runs | edited | `d` = 5 |
| 3 | takes `a` (1), reads `d` (2) | reruns | reads `d` from unit 2 | `a2` = 1000, `q` = 2 |
| 4 | reads `q` (3) | reruns | reads `q` from unit 3, which finished | `e` = 3 |

